@alison985 [at least one](https://github.com/dbt-labs/dbt-core/issues/7427#issuecomment-1520194576) non-Windows user was able to resolve a `External connection exception occurred: HTTPSConnectionPool ... Max retries exceeded` issue by setting the [`REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user/advanced/#ssl-cert-verification) environment variable.

Would you be willing to give that a try?

(`CURL_CA_BUNDLE` may or may not also work.)

@apolorei and @rbritto-fanduel

If you are getting this error message, it is probably an issue in your local environment rather than a bug in dbt-core.
 
Check out https://github.com/dbt-labs/dbt-core/issues/8554#issuecomment-1715874918 for some context and troubleshooting steps.
